                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32fa60e7-7700-4393-a405-52aa5b9568e9",
                                "sense_id": "8e1ed3fe-b99e-3be7-ab46-b841230c356c",
                                "text": "Der Wertebereich der Funktion f(x) = x² besteht aus allen positiven rationalen Zahlen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "168245b9-e7ef-4853-9052-6b36b1e511df",
                        "source_entry_id": "944171de-b367-3662-8e76-8480d18b2a03",
                        "source_sense_id": "8e1ed3fe-b99e-3be7-ab46-b841230c356c",
                        "source_sense_description": "möglicher Ergebnisraum einer mathematischen Funktion",
                        "target_lang_word": "codomain",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "codomain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab0a7c57-3e3f-3005-9497-124baa8134f3",
                                        "entry_id": "184e4c20-afe7-3d92-895c-a1a81c553a32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The target set into which a function is formally defined to map elements of its domain; the set denoted Y in the notation f : X → Y."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bee7cbb4-c9b4-4818-8c4f-7b18ea30e64b",
                                                "sense_id": "ab0a7c57-3e3f-3005-9497-124baa8134f3",
                                                "text": "Definition 2.5. A function is onto if each element of the codomain has at least one element of the domain assigned to it. In other words, a function is onto if the range equals the codomain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7420b61-bb27-433e-a52b-f599c9f091c2",
                                                "sense_id": "ab0a7c57-3e3f-3005-9497-124baa8134f3",
                                                "text": "Once we have described f as a function from A to B, by convention we will call B the codomain, even though other sets, of which B is a subset, could have been used.[…]If y is an element of the codomain, then y#92;in#92;mathit#123;Img#125;(f,A) iff there is some x in the domain such that f maps x to y."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0567cbc3-f372-4f8f-a9aa-b70e8d63f806",
                                                "sense_id": "ab0a7c57-3e3f-3005-9497-124baa8134f3",
                                                "text": "For example, the codomain of g(X)#61;X³ consists of all real numbers. A function links each element in its domain to some element in its codomain. Each domain element is linked to exactly one codomain element."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8585d4d-c9c2-39c5-b1d4-9c415a72bc1d",
                                        "entry_id": "184e4c20-afe7-3d92-895c-a1a81c553a32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The target set into which a function is formally defined to map elements of its domain; the set denoted Y in the notation f : X → Y.",
                                            "The set B."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "06fd75a5-1075-444c-8f69-613eacdf7b12",
                        "source_entry_id": "944171de-b367-3662-8e76-8480d18b2a03",
                        "source_sense_id": "8e1ed3fe-b99e-3be7-ab46-b841230c356c",
                        "source_sense_description": "möglicher Ergebnisraum einer mathematischen Funktion",
                        "target_lang_word": "domain",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "domain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A geographic area owned or controlled by a single person or organization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2d89e16-d59d-47f4-a02a-cd763d22036e",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "The king ruled his domain harshly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8ab33fb-56c6-4612-a87f-d4558489edce",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "Bears and other ferocious beasts resented man's intrusion into their domain; so, too, did the Blackfoot Indians and other tribes, whose savage hostility was a constant menace to the lives of the toiling engineers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3390989c-c8ad-45cb-9482-bd8c2748f178",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "Farmers account for just 1.5% of the British population, but the size of their domain – 71% of the country’s surface area is classified as farmland – has given them power over the public imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b3b0f36-2c56-4955-9fb7-e216fcf3d3b7",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "A blinded hermit in oblivion, disgraced\nLike Odysseus lost in Poseidon's endless domain\nIn a realm devoid ov solace, I roam"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A field or sphere of activity, influence or expertise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1001ed47-97a6-4bc8-aee8-1da3870787bb",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "Dealing with complaints isn't really my domain: get in touch with customer services."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efc64990-921f-4801-bd67-004a39810610",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "His domain is English history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "436c6d96-3ab1-43c1-a519-95eb8349da84",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "When examining studies that assess independent living and social skills—key areas of focus in adulthood for individuals with ASD—it is observed that most research evaluates only one of these domains, either activities of daily living or social functioning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "156de277-f0c2-327b-a80f-a98b59da79c5",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of related items, topics, or subjects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce94ce98-d9ca-446b-8c86-66312b66e096",
                                                "sense_id": "156de277-f0c2-327b-a80f-a98b59da79c5",
                                                "text": "Some of the most beautiful and thus appealing physical theories, including quantum electrodynamics and quantum gravity, have been dogged for decades by infinities that erupt when theorists try to prod their calculations into new domains. Getting rid of these nagging infinities has probably occupied far more effort than was spent in originating the theories."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b67a4965-40ae-3ed4-84dd-3d5e4578dd33",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of input (argument) values for which a function is defined."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f0f0636-1cd9-37f5-9e6e-e202deba1de6",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of input (argument) values for which a function is defined.",
                                            "The set A; The subset of A consisting of elements a of A such that there exists an element b in B with (a,b) in R."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "411bed4b-44cc-3d90-babe-b6c52623a222",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ring with no zero divisors; that is, in which no product of nonzero elements is zero."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "682dfb75-d39d-31e9-a9b8-40ec50104f8a",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An open and connected set in some topology. For example, the interval (0,1) as a subset of the real numbers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c783d5f-faae-39f5-a786-4540191b837f",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any DNS domain name, particularly one which has been delegated and has become representative of the delegated domain name and its subdomains."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "476a9cbb-6a62-451f-a144-8f4200cb6619",
                                                "sense_id": "2c783d5f-faae-39f5-a786-4540191b837f",
                                                "text": "2000, BIND 9 Administrator Reference Manual (9.3.2), Internet Software Consortium https://web.archive.org/web/20060619063455/http://www.bind9.net/manual/bind/9.3.2/Bv9ARM.ch01.html\nEvery name in the DNS tree is a domain, even if it is terminal, that is, has no subdomains."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18d690a9-a6b3-3aa3-9e1d-f369c6e87d3f",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of DNS or DNS-like domain names consisting of a delegated domain name and all its subdomains."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "208af736-3273-3ff5-be5b-361a4277c331",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of information having to do with a domain, the computers named in the domain, and the network on which the computers named in the domain reside."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2aea5249-69af-3b82-ba61-b98db1c3b0fc",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The collection of computers identified by a domain's domain names."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "270fef67-a7d6-312a-8140-c6a653461c3c",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small region of a magnetic material with a consistent magnetization direction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36714da7-af45-3fb1-bc75-12d9d881f2a3",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Such a region used as a data storage element in a bubble memory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef594b54-ee4b-3c91-9e4a-16b45996e1e5",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of technical metadata that represent the type of a data item, its characteristics, name, and usage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "585adb7a-951e-45b9-bcdc-cc808aa53322",
                                                "sense_id": "ef594b54-ee4b-3c91-9e4a-16b45996e1e5",
                                                "text": "A characteristic of a field. A data domain specifies a data type and applies the minimum and maximum values allowed and other constraints."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "545c3ef5-8b2c-3a76-8cf9-125a69dcf1a2",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The highest rank in the classification of organisms, above kingdom; in the three-domain system, one of the taxa Bacteria, Archaea, or Eukaryota."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25f0f953-87a6-3d0b-92fd-d74086c6d2e4",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A folded section of a protein molecule that has a discrete function; the equivalent section of a chromosome."
                                        ],
